# End-to-End Feature Creation Guide

> When adding a complete feature, create files in this order to avoid gaps.
> Examples below use **Client** as a representative module — adapt names to your actual feature.

## API Conventions

- Keep all API functions in \`src/api/\`, split by business module
- **Do not** call \`fetch\`/\`axios.get\` directly in components/stores — use wrapper functions

> ⚠️ Could not auto-detect the project's HTTP client wrapper.

## Standard Steps

### 1. Type Definitions

\`\`\`ts
// src/types/client.ts
export interface ClientItem {
  id: string;
  name: string;
  // ...actual project fields
}

export interface ClientListParams {
  page: number;
  pageSize: number;
}
\`\`\`

### 2. API Functions

\`\`\`ts
// src/api/client.ts
import type { ClientItem, ClientListParams } from "@/types/client";


export const fetchClientList = (params: ClientListParams) => {
  return apiClient.get<ClientItem[]>("/clients", { params });
};
\`\`\`

### 3. Store（Zustand）

\`\`\`ts
// src/store/clientStore.ts
import { create } from "zustand";
import type { ClientItem } from "@/types/client";
import { fetchClientList } from "@/api/client";

interface ClientStore {
  items: ClientItem[];
  loading: boolean;
  fetchItems: () => Promise<void>;
}

export const useClientStore = create<ClientStore>((set) => ({
  items: [],
  loading: false,
  fetchItems: async () => {
    set({ loading: true });
    const items = await fetchClientList();
    set({ items, loading: false });
  },
}));
\`\`\`


### 4. Reusable Hook (Optional)

\`\`\`ts
// src/hooks/useClientList.ts
import { useEffect } from "react";
import { useClientStore } from "@/store/clientStore";

export function useClientList() {
  const { items, loading, fetchItems } = useClientStore();

  useEffect(() => {
    void fetchItems();
  }, [fetchItems]);

  return { items, loading, error: null };
}
\`\`\`


### 5. Page Component

\`\`\`tsx
// src/pages/ClientList/ClientList.tsx
import { useClientList } from "@/hooks/useClientList";

export function ClientList() {
  const { items, loading, error } = useClientList({ page: 1, pageSize: 20 });

  if (loading) return <div>Loading...</div>;
  if (error) return <div>{error}</div>;
  if (!items.length) return <div>No data</div>;
  return <ul>{items.map((item) => <li key={item.id}>{item.name}</li>)}</ul>;
}
\`\`\`

### 6. Route Registration

\`\`\`tsx
// src/index.tsx or route config file
{ path: "/clients", element: <ClientList /> }
{ path: "/clients/:id", element: <ClientDetail /> }
\`\`\`

## File Checklist

After adding a feature, confirm the following files were created/updated:

- [ ] \`src/types/client.ts\` — Type definitions
- [ ] \`src/api/client.ts\` — API functions
- [ ] \`src/store/clientStore.ts\` — Store
- [ ] \`src/hooks/useClientList.ts\` — Data hook (optional)
- [ ] \`src/pages/ClientList/ClientList.tsx\` — Page component
- [ ] Route config updated

### Verification

- [ ] All files from the checklist above exist at the expected paths
- [ ] Route is registered and navigable
- [ ] Loading, empty, and error states are handled in the page component
- [ ] Run \`npm run type-check\` — no errors
- [ ] Run \`npm run test\` — all tests pass

---

*Follow this pattern for project consistency. See @project-structure.mdc for actual directory locations.*
